\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid14240563\charrsid14292503 \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 
* Comment-1: These three factors (formal education, years of professional work experience, and hours of company-funded training) together account for 56.1% of the variation in salary, which we found from the value of R square.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Comment-2: The estimated change in annual salary associated with one additional year of education, holding experience and training constant is 1895 USD on average.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Comment-3: The estimated change in annual salary associated with one additional year of experience, holding year of education and training constant is 1217 USD on average.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Comment-4: From regression analysis, we can see that the estimated change in annua\hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 
l salary associated with one additional hour of company-funded training, holding other factors constant is 76 USD on average.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * For this specific factor, t(246) = 2.604, p = .010, which is statistically significant at 5% level of significance.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Thus we can conclude that, even though the increase in salary for one additional hour of company-funded training isn't that much compared to one unit of change in other factors, it's still statistically significant.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Which means the money currently spent on training is associated with measurably higher pay.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14240563 
\par 
\par 
