\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9111546 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9111546 \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Encoding: UTF-8.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 PRESERVE.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 SET DECIMAL DOT.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Since I messed up while generating the output of my first assignment, I'll be properly segmenting my code so that the final output is clean and reproducible using whatever syntax I used during data analysis.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Step-1: Data loading/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 GET DATA  /TYPE=TXT
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /FILE="E:\\Statistical Softwares\\SPSS\\CUSPC-SPSS\\Class-7\\salary regression data.csv"
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /ENCODING='UTF8'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /DELIMITERS=","
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /QUALIFIER='"'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /ARRANGEMENT=DELIMITED
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /FIRSTCASE=2
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /DATATYPEMIN PERCENTAGE=95.0
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /VARIABLES=
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   employee_id AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   age AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   education_years AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   experience_years AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   training_hours AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   region AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   annual_salary_k AUTO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /MAP.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 RESTORE.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 CACHE.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 EXECUTE.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 DATASET NAME DataSet1 WINDOW=FRONT.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Step-2: Data labelling/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 VARIABLE LABELS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     employee_id 'Anonymised employee identifier'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     age 'Age at time of extract (Years)'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     education_years 'Total years of completed formal education (Years)'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     experience_years 'Total years of professional work experience (Years)'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     training_hours 'Company-funded training received in the last 12 months (Hours)'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     region 'Office location type (Urban/Suburban/Rural)'
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     annual_salary_k 'Gross annual salary (USD thousands)'.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 EXECUTE.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 VARIABLE LEVEL employee_id (NOMINAL).
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 EXECUTE.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Step-3: Data Checking/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 DATASET ACTIVATE DataSet1.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 FREQUENCIES VARIABLES=employee_id age education_years experience_years training_hours region 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     annual_salary_k
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /FORMAT=NOTABLE
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /STATISTICS=RANGE MINIMUM MAXIMUM
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /ORDER=ANALYSIS.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 FREQUENCIES VARIABLES=region
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /ORDER=ANALYSIS.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * All 250 observations are present in the given dataset, and no impossible values were found. We can safely proceed to the next steps of analysis.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Task 1/
\par .
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Custom Tables.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 CTABLES
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /VLABELS VARIABLES=\hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 age education_years experience_years training_hours annual_salary_k 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     DISPLAY=LABEL
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /TABLE age [COUNT 'Complete cases (n)' F40.0, MINIMUM, MAXIMUM, MEAN, MEDIAN, STDDEV] + 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     education_years [COUNT 'Complete cases (n)' F40.0, MINIMUM, MAXIMUM, MEAN, MEDIAN, STDDEV] + 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     experience_years [COUNT 'Complete cases (n)' F40.0, MINIMUM, MAXIMUM, MEAN, MEDIAN, STDDEV] + 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     training_hours [COUNT 'Complete cases (n)' F40.0, MINIMUM, MAXIMUM, MEAN, MEDIAN, STDDEV] + 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     annual_salary_k [COUNT 'Complete cases (n)' F40.0, MINIMUM, MAXIMUM, MEAN, MEDIAN, STDDEV]
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /CRITERIA CILEVEL=95.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Task 2/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Graph-2a/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Chart Builder.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 GGRAPH
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRAPHDATASET NAME="graphdataset" VARIABLES=annual_salary_k MISSING=LISTWISE REPORTMISSING=NO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRAPHSPEC SOURCE=INLINE
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /FRAME OUTER=NO INNER=NO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRIDLINES XAXIS=NO YAXIS=YES
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /STYLE GRADIENT=NO.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 BEGIN GPL
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   SOURCE: s=userSource(id("graphdataset"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   DATA: annual_salary_k=col(source(s), name("annual_salary_k"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   GUIDE: axis(dim(1), label("Gross annual salary (USD thousands)"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   GUIDE: axis(dim(2), label("Frequency"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   GUIDE: text.title(label("Histogram of Gross annual salary (USD thousands)"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   ELEMENT: interval(position(summary.count(bin.rect(annual_salary_k))), 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     shape.interior(shape.square))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 END GPL.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Graph-2b/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Chart Builder.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 GGRAPH
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRAPHDATASET NAME="graphdataset" VARIABLES=region COUNT()[name="COUNT"] MISSING=LISTWISE 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     REPORTMISSING=NO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRAPHSPEC SOURCE=INLINE
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /FRAME OUTER=NO INNER=NO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRIDLINES XAXIS=NO YAXIS=YES
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /STYLE GRADIENT=NO.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 BEGIN GPL
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   SOURCE: s=userSource(id("graphdataset"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   DATA: region=col(source(s), name("region"), unit.category())
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   DATA: COUNT=col(source(s), name("COUNT"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   GUIDE: axis(dim(1), label("Office location type (Urban/Suburban/Rural)"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   GUIDE: axis(dim(2), label("Percent"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   GUIDE: text.title(label("Bar chart of Office location type (Urban/Suburban/Rural)"))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   SCALE: linear(dim(2), include(0))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   EL\hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 EMENT: interval(position(summary.percent(region*COUNT, base.all(acrossPanels()))), 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     shape.interior(shape.square))
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 END GPL.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Graph-2c/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Chart Builder.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 GGRAPH
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRAPHDATASET NAME="graphdataset" VARIABLES=region annual_salary_k MISSING=LISTWISE 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     REPORTMISSING=NO
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /GRAPHSPEC SOURCE=INLINE
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /FRAME OUTER=NO INNER=NO
