\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Main Table/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 CORRELATIONS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /VARIABLES=age education_years experience_years training_hours annual_salary_k
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /PRINT=TWOTAIL NOSIG FULL
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /MISSING=PAIRWISE.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2  
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Correlation Matrix/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 CORRELATIONS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /VARIABLES=age education_years experience_years training_hours annual_salary_k
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /PRINT=TWOTAIL NOSIG LOWER
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /MISSING=PAIRWISE.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 OUTPUT MODIFY
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /SELECT TABLES
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /IF COMMANDS=["Correlations(LAST)"]
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     SUBTYPES=["Correlations"]
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /TABLECELLS SELECT=[SIGNIFICANCE COUNT]
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2              SELECTDIMENSION=ROWS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2              APPLYTO=ROW
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2              HIDE=YES
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 /TABLECELLS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2       SELECT=[TITLE]
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2       REPLACE="Pearson Correlation Matrix"
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2  /TABLECELLS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     SELECT=["CORRELATION"]
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     SELECTDIMENSION=ROWS
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     APPLYTO=ROWHEADER
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2     HIDE=YES.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * /Task 4/
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 REGRESSION
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /MISSING LISTWISE
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /STATISTICS COEFF OUTS CI(95) R ANOVA
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /CRITERIA=PIN(.05) POUT(.10)
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /NOORIGIN 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /DEPENDENT annual_salary_k
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2   /METHOD=ENTER education_years experience_years training_hours.
\par 
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 
* Comment-1: These three factors (formal education, years of professional work experience, and hours of company-funded training) together account for 56.1% of the variation in salary, which we found from the value of R square.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Comment-2: The estimated change in annual salary associated with one additional year of education, holding experience and training constant is 1895 USD on average.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Comment-3: The estimated change in annual salary associated with one additional year of experience, holding year of education and training constant is 1217 USD on average.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Comment-4: From regression analysis, we can see that the estimated change in annual salary associated with one additional hour of company-funded training, holding other factors constant is 76 USD on average.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * For this specific factor, t(246) = 2.604, p = .010, which is statistically significant at 5% level of significance.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Thus we can conclude that, even though the increase \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 
in salary for one additional hour of company-funded training isn't that much compared to one unit of change in other factors, it's still statistically significant.
\par \hich\af2\dbch\af31505\loch\f2 * Which means the money currently spent on training is associated with measurably higher pay.
\par 
